# 6. Data Structure

Each running activity stores the following information.

| Field | Required | Description |
|---|---|---|
| Title | Yes | Defaults to "Outdoor run" |
| Description | No | Additional activity notes |
| Location | No | Plain text location |
| Date | Yes | Activity date |
| Time | Yes | Activity start time |
| Distance | Yes | Distance in kilometers |
| Duration | Yes | Moving duration |
| Pace | Calculated | Displayed in minutes per kilometer |
| Average heart rate | Conditional | Required for manual entry; may be missing in imported activities |
| Score | Conditional | Automatically calculated when heart rate is available |
| Elevation gain | No | Meters |
| Cadence | No | Steps per minute |

### Input behavior

Distance, duration, and pace are interconnected.

- Changing distance recalculates pace.
- Changing duration recalculates pace.
- Changing pace recalculates distance.
- Duration remains as entered when pace is changed.

The interface should use simple number inputs, date and time pickers, and suitable duration controls.

### Manual entry requirements

Manual run entry requires:

- Title.
- Date.
- Time.
- Distance.
- Duration.
- Pace.
- Average heart rate.

Optional fields:

- Description.
- Location.
- Elevation gain.
- Cadence.

Pace, distance, and duration must remain synchronized.

