# 14. Rules and Edge Cases

### Overlapping runs

Each run occupies a time range from its start time to its start time plus moving duration.

A new or edited run cannot overlap another run.

The app blocks the save and explains the conflict.

Multiple runs on the same day are allowed when their time ranges do not overlap.

### Missing heart rate

Manual entries require heart rate.

Imported runs may have missing heart-rate data.

Such activities remain visible but do not receive a score until heart rate is entered.

### Unusual values

Unusual values are accepted without warnings.

There is no outlier detection or automatic rejection based on unusual pace or heart-rate values in version 1.

### Empty periods

Score chart:

- Skip periods without eligible scores.
- Connect surrounding points.

Volume chart:

- Show zero for periods without runs.

Empty periods are excluded from score averages.

### No activities

The dashboard displays its empty state.

The user can still add or import activities.

### First activity

The first recorded run is the beginning of the user's running progress history.

The chart starts from the earliest recorded run.

### Time grouping

- Weeks start on Monday.
- Quarters follow calendar quarters.
- Distances use kilometers.
- Pace uses minutes per kilometer.

