# 15. Account and Authentication

### Authentication

Google sign-in is the only authentication method in version 1.

The user's name and email come from Google sign-in.

The name is used in the dashboard welcome message.

### Account menu

The account menu contains:

- Manage account.
- Settings.
- Log out.
- Delete account.

### Manage account

Users can:

- View their Google account name.
- View their Google email address.
- Upload an optional avatar.

The app should not request unnecessary personal information.

### Settings

Settings contain:

- Privacy Policy.
- Terms and Conditions.
- Guides.

Guides include:

- How to import running activities.
- How the score works.

### Delete account

Users must be able to permanently delete their account.

Deletion must remove:

- Their account.
- Their running activities.
- Their stored avatar and other associated user data.

The implementation must ensure that deletion is handled securely and that the actual deletion behavior matches the promises made in the Terms and Privacy Policy.

